{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg encoding pipeline jpeg encoding pipeline","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md","fileName":"JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"JPEG Encoding Pipeline","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[JPEG Compression Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["JPEG Compression Forensics","JPEG Signature","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"jpeg encoding pipeline jpeg encoding pipeline","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md","fileName":"JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"JPEG Encoding Pipeline","heading":"JPEG Encoding Pipeline","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The JPEG encoding pipeline first converts RGB pixels to luminance and chrominance channels and may downsample the color channels. It centers the values, divides each channel into 8-by-8 blocks, and applies a discrete cosine transform to express every block as spatial-frequency coefficients.\n\nFrequency-dependent quantization performs the lossy step by rounding those coefficients. Zigzag ordering, run-length representation, and Huffman coding then exploit the many resulting zeros and repeated symbols without adding further loss. The chosen tables and packaging help form a [[JPEG Signature]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["JPEG Compression Forensics","JPEG Signature","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/JPEG Encoding Pipeline.md::2","so